# The two ONNX encoders (87 MB and 70 MB) are committed as ordinary git blobs.
# Both are under GitHub's 100 MB per-file hard limit, so no Git LFS is required —
# `git clone` just downloads them. GitHub will print a >50 MB advisory on push.
#
# They are immutable release artefacts, so history will not grow from them. If a
# future model ever exceeds 100 MB, or you simply prefer LFS, convert with:
#
#   git lfs install
#   git lfs track "*.onnx" "*.so"
#   git lfs migrate import --include="*.onnx,*.so" --everything   # rewrites history
#   git push --force-with-lease
#
# (That rewrite changes every commit hash, so coordinate it with anyone who has cloned.)

# treat the binary artefacts as binary: no diffing, no eol munging
*.onnx binary
*.so binary
*.pkl binary
*.ckpt binary
*.png binary
*.bin binary

# normalise line endings for text
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
